course: dictionary
lesson: 10367
title: One word, many trays
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may know a tray as a flat board with low edges for carrying food, cups or plates. Context tells you which meaning is meant. In «She carried the tray of tea to Grandma's room», the words carried and tea show it is a tray for carrying things.
explain: One word can mean different things in different places. A baking tray is a flat metal sheet for baking in the oven. An ice cube tray holds water to freeze into cubes. A tray on a desk holds papers. Read the words around the word, then pick the meaning that fits.
explain: Maths uses tray too. «816 eggs in trays of 24» means each tray holds 24 eggs, so you can find the number of trays by dividing. Check your answer by multiplying back: 24 × 34 = 816, so there are 34 trays.
fact: A tray is a flat board with low edges for carrying or holding things.
fact: A tray can be used to carry food, cups or plates.
fact: A baking tray is a flat metal sheet for baking in the oven.
fact: An ice cube tray holds water to freeze into cubes.
fact: In maths, trays can show equal groups: total = trays × per tray.
exercise: «Ali carried a tray of cups and plates to the table.» What is a tray here? | A deep hole in the ground | A loud drum | *A flat board with low edges for carrying things | A small room with a window
exercise: «She took the tray of biscuits out of the oven.» Which kind of tray is this? | A tray on a desk for papers | An ice cube tray | A tray of water for a pet | *A baking tray, a flat metal sheet for baking
exercise: There are 4 trays with 6 muffins on each tray. How many muffins are there altogether? | *24 | 10 | 46 | 18
test:
«The water froze in the ice cube tray overnight.» What does the tray hold? | Paint for art | Papers for school | *Water to freeze into cubes | Seeds for the garden
«Ava sets up two seed trays instead.» What is a seed tray used for? | Carrying lunch to class | *Growing seeds | Holding papers on a desk | Baking cakes in an oven
exam:
In «The papers sat in the tray on his desk», what is a tray? | A flat metal sheet for baking | A flat board for carrying food | *A container that holds papers | A dish for holding ice
